## Commands
- `kbdoc --overview`: how many triples, the relations, the papers and the interpretations.
- `kbdoc "words" [-k {{ max_hits }}] [--offset N]`: triples ranked by these words (subject, relation, object, passage).
- `kbdoc --predicate NAME [--paper ID] [--interpretation ID] [--offset N]`: the triples of one relation, a page at a time.
- `kbdoc --id TRIPLE_ID ...`: these triples with their full evidence.
- `kbcheck`: checks answer.json.

Each command runs in a new shell; files you write in the current directory stay. The run ends after {{ step_limit }} replies (model calls).

